          "message": {
            "text": "DM-2291: A one-run primary-key shortcut is only valid for the primary instance's ordinary layout. Decomposed assignments and HarfBuzz shaping views carry run-level shaping semantics (notably Blink's explicit script tag and syllabic dotted-circle insertion), so routing them through singleFontMarkup can silently replace the selected shaping engine even though the font key is unchanged. Keep those runs on the run-text emitter; this is an engine/assignment invariant rather than a codepoint exception.",
