          "message": {
            "text": "Per-glyph ownership spans come from HarfBuzz cluster boundaries, not Glyph.codePoints: repeated clusters share one span, the next distinct cluster fixes its UTF-16 end, and the legacy cursor handles absent cluster data in either direction. Focused controls cover astral text, ligatures, reversed native-direction shaping, and clusterless RTL; this prevents an empty space beside an inked letter from being falsely attributed to the whole run.",
            "markdown": "Per-glyph ownership spans come from HarfBuzz cluster boundaries, not Glyph.codePoints: repeated clusters share one span, the next distinct cluster fixes its UTF-16 end, and the legacy cursor handles absent cluster data in either direction. Focused controls cover astral text, ligatures, reversed native-direction shaping, and clusterless RTL; this prevents an empty space beside an inked letter from being falsely attributed to the whole run."
          },
          "locations": [
